{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Every vow, and every binding oath, to afflict the soul</b> – Since it stated that the husband may annul, one might think all vows are included in the implication? Scripture therefore says \"to afflict the soul\" – he may annul only vows of affliction of soul, and these are explained in tractate Nedarim. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 30:14). And the Rav spoke in abbreviated language, for the husband may annul vows of affliction of soul, and these are of the type such as \"the fruits of the world are forbidden to me,\" and even if she vowed not to taste even one of all the species (Tosefta Nedarim 7:3), and he may also annul matters between himself and her even though they do not involve affliction of soul, such as \"I will not paint,\" \"I will not cosmetics,\" and \"I will not use my bed,\" and these are what Scripture refers to with \"between a man and his wife\" (Numbers 30:17), as is explained in the last chapter of Nedarim (79a). And the same ruling applies to the father himself, as it is taught in the Sifrei (Matot 157): \"I have only a husband, who may annul only vows between himself and her and vows that involve affliction of soul – from where do we derive the father? You reason, etc.\" — until \"before I merited to derive it, Scripture says: 'These are the statutes which HaShem commanded Moses, between a man and his wife, between a father and his daughter' (Numbers 30:17) – perforce you liken the father to the husband: just as the husband may annul only matters between himself and her and matters that involve affliction of soul, so too the father may annul only matters between himself and her and matters that involve affliction of soul.\" And so it is also taught in the Gemara of the Jerusalem Talmud (Nedarim 11:1):"], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The Sifrei citation 'מטות כז' is rendered as section 157 following the standard numbering of Sifrei Zuta on Matot; the section number in the Hebrew appears to follow an alternative enumeration."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:42.522106796Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}